# Line endings for the Inform regression harness.
#
# glulxe reads each test script line as one command. A trailing CR becomes part
# of the command ("s\r"), so every turn answers "I beg your pardon?" and the
# whole case fails. Transcripts are diffed against glulxe output, which is
# always LF. Both therefore have to stay strictly LF, regardless of the
# developer's core.autocrlf setting.
SoMe-Universe-IF.inform/Tests/Cases/*.txt text eol=lf
SoMe-Universe-IF.inform/Tests/Ideals/*.txt text eol=lf

# Story source is fed to the Inform 7 compiler; keep it LF too so that a
# checkout on another machine cannot change the compiled output.
SoMe-Universe-IF.inform/Source/story.ni text eol=lf

# Only the paths above are pinned; everything else keeps the platform default.
